(6353669, 940840, 69324, '<td valign="top">I much more prefer Librodos work that brings out the true essence of the individual, sans all the props. This image epitomizes that criteria, by far my favorite in the challenge. Thanks for submitting.</td>', 'I much more prefer Librodos work that brings out the true essence of the individual, sans all the props. This image epitomizes that criteria, by far my favorite in the challenge. Thanks for submitting.', '2011-03-16 18:51:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(6353672, 940739, 74911, '<td valign="top">Like the use of dappled light. The simplicity of the image works very well... I see the strain due to light falling on her right eye...and that gives a slight discomfort while viewing (a shrink in the middle of the forehead)</td>', 'Like the use of dappled light. The simplicity of the image works very well... I see the strain due to light falling on her right eye...and that gives a slight discomfort while viewing (a shrink in the middle of the forehead)', '2011-03-16 18:54:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(6353673, 940964, 74911, '<td valign="top">Librodo effect is certainly evident... I like the reduced saturation. I would like to see the tattoo on his right arm to be in focus too. And also, the focus on the face is sharp. I can see how you have blurred the rest of the image to lay emphasis on the eye. But, IMO it is slightly overdone and as a result, the blur does not smoothly transitio from the sharper areas.<br/> <br/>I am sure this image does well in this challenge.<br/> <br/>Raj</td>', 'Librodo effect is certainly evident... I like the reduced saturation. I would like to see the tattoo on his right arm to be in focus too. And also, the focus on the face is sharp. I can see how you have blurred the rest of the image to lay emphasis on the eye. But, IMO it is slightly overdone and as a result, the blur does not smoothly transitio from the sharper areas. I am sure this image does well in this challenge. Raj', '2011-03-16 18:57:44.000000', NULL, 1),
