(6354661, 940556, 113419, '<td valign="top">Very nicely done black and white.  Wonderful focus on the face.  Fabulous depth of field.  Good all around photo - why oh why isn''t it bigger?</td>', 'Very nicely done black and white.  Wonderful focus on the face.  Fabulous depth of field.  Good all around photo - why oh why isn''t it bigger?', '2011-03-17 13:30:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(6354667, 940655, 53147, '<td valign="top">Hey Steve. I voted this a 6. <i>The good</i> - your model certainly has lovely eyes. They don''t feel overly pimped out but pretty much just right. Her makeup job is lovely as well (good match with the veil) and the doodad on her forehead is a nice touch. IMO a very good edit job on her face. Bouncing back and forth from another image it seems that her skin tone may be just a tad bit on the orange side. <i>The indifferent </i>- her pose for some reason just feels a bit static and unconnecting. It''s not terrible, but she just doesn''t seem to be connecting with me. Feels a bit too generic and unemotional. Maybe some slight angle so that she is pushed into having to look into the lens, either from slightly above or from an angle rather than just setting her right in front. Librodo often comes at you from an interesting angle. <i>The bad</i> - that green is wretched on my monitor. You have this lovely model with great sharpness and color balance between her eyes and the veil and then this bright flourescent green background that totally for the most part steals the attention away from her eyes. It is just too much. My choice probably would have been a darker more muted background. Black probably would have been very nice to make sure that the focus was directed towards her eyes and the lovely colors of purple rather than away. Hope that helps.</td>', 'Hey Steve. I voted this a 6. The good - your model certainly has lovely eyes. They don''t feel overly pimped out but pretty much just right. Her makeup job is lovely as well (good match with the veil) and the doodad on her forehead is a nice touch. IMO a very good edit job on her face. Bouncing back and forth from another image it seems that her skin tone may be just a tad bit on the orange side. The indifferent - her pose for some reason just feels a bit static and unconnecting. It''s not terrible, but she just doesn''t seem to be connecting with me. Feels a bit too generic and unemotional. Maybe some slight angle so that she is pushed into having to look into the lens, either from slightly above or from an angle rather than just setting her right in front. Librodo often comes at you from an interesting angle. The bad - that green is wretched on my monitor. You have this lovely model with great sharpness and color balance between her eyes and the veil and then this bright flourescent green background that totally for the most part steals the attention away from her eyes. It is just too much. My choice probably would have been a darker more muted background. Black probably would have been very nice to make sure that the focus was directed towards her eyes and the lovely colors of purple rather than away. Hope that helps.', '2011-03-17 13:33:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(6354700, 939911, 129313, '<td valign="top">The colors, the contrast, the sharpness, and the model.. truly, librodorized!! :)</td>', 'The colors, the contrast, the sharpness, and the model.. truly, librodorized!! :)', '2011-03-17 14:05:02.000000', NULL, 1),
