(6355031, 940739, 24962, '<td valign="top">Interesting! There is a certain look about this one, the lighting and the use of shadows. I have one 10 to give and you get it:)</td>', 'Interesting! There is a certain look about this one, the lighting and the use of shadows. I have one 10 to give and you get it:)', '2011-03-17 17:56:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(6355041, 940363, 53147, '<td valign="top">Hey Maria. I gave you a 7 on this shot. But looking at how I voted I only had 6 images with a higher score. So here we go. The good - lovely model. Very nice eye contact. Clean editing and pleasing light. Composition is nice. The framing of the veil works for me. The bad - nothing sticks out really. There is some weird texture going on with her nose there at the shadow line - but nothing a quick view would catch. The indifferent - the whole shot is pleasing, nothing really bad to say about it. But that is also the issue I guess. It is very nice, but doesn''t scream a big DPC "WOW". No major flaws, no major issues, but not a whole lot to grab the voter and keep them here for very long. DPC as a client, for the most part, wants and needs that instant grab. That quick fix of WOW to score that higher vote. And I think that is what you are missing here for the DPC community and a challenge with this theme. That said - print this out as an 11x14 and deliver it to your model. Her reaction should be better than any score you could receive here. I would love to be able to deliver an image like this to a client.</td>', 'Hey Maria. I gave you a 7 on this shot. But looking at how I voted I only had 6 images with a higher score. So here we go. The good - lovely model. Very nice eye contact. Clean editing and pleasing light. Composition is nice. The framing of the veil works for me. The bad - nothing sticks out really. There is some weird texture going on with her nose there at the shadow line - but nothing a quick view would catch. The indifferent - the whole shot is pleasing, nothing really bad to say about it. But that is also the issue I guess. It is very nice, but doesn''t scream a big DPC "WOW". No major flaws, no major issues, but not a whole lot to grab the voter and keep them here for very long. DPC as a client, for the most part, wants and needs that instant grab. That quick fix of WOW to score that higher vote. And I think that is what you are missing here for the DPC community and a challenge with this theme. That said - print this out as an 11x14 and deliver it to your model. Her reaction should be better than any score you could receive here. I would love to be able to deliver an image like this to a client.', '2011-03-17 17:59:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(6355042, 940677, 53147, '<td valign="top">Her smile just lights up this image. I feel she is smiling at me rather than at the camera. Lovely.</td>', 'Her smile just lights up this image. I feel she is smiling at me rather than at the camera. Lovely.', '2011-03-17 18:00:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(6355046, 940353, 53147, '<td valign="top">Love the lens flare. Seems a bit too much canvas on the left, but a lovely image overall.</td>', 'Love the lens flare. Seems a bit too much canvas on the left, but a lovely image overall.', '2011-03-17 18:00:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(6355047, 940778, 53147, '<td valign="top">Interesting choices for you to go with. A guy instead of a girl. Muted tones instead of vibrant colors. And even with the "veil", you chose one with no color or distinct pattern. And yet it still has your fingerprints all over it Manny. I am looking forward to seeing how you fare against all of us copycats.</td>', 'Interesting choices for you to go with. A guy instead of a girl. Muted tones instead of vibrant colors. And even with the "veil", you chose one with no color or distinct pattern. And yet it still has your fingerprints all over it Manny. I am looking forward to seeing how you fare against all of us copycats.', '2011-03-17 18:00:45.000000', NULL, 1),
